instr:
`decodeModeSMessage()` throws `not implemented` for captured ADS-B traffic

I hit this while replaying a dump1090-fa capture through `@squawk/mode-s` to inspect aircraft position and altitude.

```typescript
import { decodeModeSMessage } from '@squawk/mode-s';
const bytes = Uint8Array.from(Buffer.from('8DAB096958C90106E9199E88D1A5', 'hex'));
const message = decodeModeSMessage(bytes);
if (message?.kind === 'extendedSquitterPosition') {
  console.log({ address: message.icaoHex, altitude: message.baroAltitudeFt });
}
```

I expected a decoded position report, following the API doc comments and the "Usage" and "API" sections of `packages/libs/mode-s/README.md`. Instead, importing the package or calling its decoders throws `Error: not implemented`.

Could you fill in the remaining decoding stubs under `packages/libs/mode-s/src/`? They are in `message.ts`, `frame.ts`, `acas.ts`, `altitude.ts`, `bits.ts`, `comm-b.ts`, `cpr.ts`, `emergency-status.ts`, `flight-status.ts`, `identification.ts`, `identity.ts`, `mode-ac.ts`, `operational-status.ts`, `surface-movement.ts`, `surveillance-status.ts`, `target-state-status.ts`, and `velocity.ts`. This includes the separately exported field decoders, Mode A/C replies, and airborne/surface CPR position resolution as well as whole-message decoding. The existing doc comments describe the expected behavior for each entry point.

